From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:30:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] hwdec_cuda: add --cuda-primary-context

The CUDA hwdec interop creates a CUDA context for every render context
(cuCtxCreate), and the copy hwdecs let FFmpeg create one per decoder.
Each costs device memory: about 160 MiB on an RTX 3070 Ti. A libmpv
client that plays several videos in one process (for example a
compositor or a scene renderer with several video textures) pays that
once per player, although nothing stops the players from sharing one.

With --cuda-primary-context, the GL and Vulkan interops retain the
device's primary context instead (cuDevicePrimaryCtxRetain) and release
it on uninit, so every player in the process shares that one context
and mpv never destroys a context it did not create. The copy hwdecs
pass FFmpeg's equivalent primary_ctx option to av_hwdevice_ctx_create.
The default stays a private context per player.

Origin: ours
Why: liascape docs/decisions.md "Share one CUDA context across a scene's videos by patching mpv"
Status: candidate-for-upstream
---
 .../cuda-primary-context.txt                  |  1 +
 DOCS/man/options.rst                          | 12 ++++
 options/options.c                             |  1 +
 options/options.h                             |  1 +
 video/cuda.c                                  |  8 ++-
 video/out/hwdec/hwdec_cuda.c                  | 60 ++++++++++++++++++-
 video/out/hwdec/hwdec_cuda.h                  |  9 +++
 video/out/hwdec/hwdec_cuda_gl.c               | 11 ++--
 video/out/hwdec/hwdec_cuda_vk.c               |  6 +-
 9 files changed, 97 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 DOCS/interface-changes/cuda-primary-context.txt

diff --git a/DOCS/interface-changes/cuda-primary-context.txt b/DOCS/interface-changes/cuda-primary-context.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..94bea1c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DOCS/interface-changes/cuda-primary-context.txt
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+add `--cuda-primary-context`
diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index fa71dc0..237e5e7 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -1571,6 +1571,18 @@ Video
     For the Vulkan GPU backend, decoding must always happen on the display
     device, and this option has no effect.
 
+``--cuda-primary-context=<yes|no>``
+    Use the CUDA device's primary context for the ``cuda`` and ``nvdec``
+    hwdecs (with both the OpenGL and Vulkan GPU backends) and for the
+    ``cuda-copy`` and ``nvdec-copy`` hwdecs, instead of creating a context of
+    their own (default: no).
+
+    Every CUDA context costs device memory (on the order of 100-200 MiB),
+    while a device has only one primary context per process. This helps
+    libmpv clients that run several players or render contexts in one process:
+    with this option they all share that one context. mpv only retains and
+    releases the primary context, so a client that uses it too keeps it.
+
 ``--vaapi-device=<device file|adapter name>``
     Choose the DRM device for ``vaapi-copy``. This should be the path to a
     DRM device file. (Default: ``/dev/dri/renderD128``)
